WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:05.730
<b>Understood.</b>

00:00.890 --> 00:02.160
Understood.

00:02.730 --> 00:05.730
<b>Yes.</b>

00:02.940 --> 00:03.780
Yes.

00:03.310 --> 00:05.730
<b>Please be careful, 
Rampo-san.</b>

00:03.780 --> 00:05.430
Please be careful, Rampo-san.

00:09.190 --> 00:12.850
We'll rendezvous with 
Rampo-san at Runway 122R.

00:13.370 --> 00:14.690
Let's go.

00:14.690 --> 00:15.670
Indeed.

00:16.100 --> 00:18.630
Now, then, give me a ride 
on the tiger's back!

00:18.630 --> 00:18.990
Huh?

00:19.300 --> 00:21.200
You are the Hunting Dogs' servant!

00:21.200 --> 00:25.050
Thus, from now on, you are our car!

00:25.050 --> 00:26.750
Dogs riding cats!

00:27.830 --> 00:29.440
What a hoot!

00:29.440 --> 00:31.460
I'm a tiger, not a cat.

00:31.800 --> 00:33.400
I just realized...

00:33.400 --> 00:36.370
I don't like dealing with these 
kinds of people in general.

00:40.150 --> 00:41.230
Now, go!

00:41.230 --> 00:43.650
This airport is a giant amusement park!

00:43.650 --> 00:45.490
All right, fine.

00:45.490 --> 00:47.750
But please cooperate with us.

00:48.130 --> 00:49.510
Cooperate?

00:49.510 --> 00:50.650
You know...

00:50.650 --> 00:54.360
Convince the others not to 
attack the Detective Agency.

00:54.360 --> 00:57.730
Of course, I'll instruct my 
henchmen appropriately by radio.

00:57.730 --> 01:01.150
But Tetchou aside, Jouno is missing.

01:01.650 --> 01:03.260
I can't guarantee anything.

01:04.600 --> 01:07.910
Although, Rampo-san did 
deduce that he'd be missing.

01:08.600 --> 01:09.550
Huh?

01:10.230 --> 01:13.560
Jouno-san was defeated by the 
vampires and taken away...

01:13.560 --> 01:15.640
That's what Rampo-san deduced.

01:16.130 --> 01:20.550
And the enemy announced that it 
was the Detective Agency's doing.

01:20.870 --> 01:22.390
Which means it doesn't make sense...

01:23.000 --> 01:26.770
that you would tell me 
 Jouno-san's missing.

01:27.310 --> 01:29.050
How could such an inconsistency happen?

01:29.720 --> 01:32.520
No matter what we'd done with Jouno-san,

01:32.520 --> 01:35.010
you would have attacked me for it.

01:35.410 --> 01:37.680
What, is that what you were worrying about?

01:38.730 --> 01:40.920
The Detectives got that one wrong.

01:41.490 --> 01:42.950
I'll tell you how later.

01:43.710 --> 01:45.940
Rampo-san doesn't get things wrong.

01:49.140 --> 01:50.630
Well, shucks.

01:51.570 --> 01:54.460
Normally, I'm the one making people fess up.

01:54.910 --> 01:57.180
You're rather difficult, aren't you?

02:04.200 --> 02:06.140
Copper whip, Ajuga blossom.

02:07.000 --> 02:08.780
<i>Sh-She got me!</i>

02:08.780 --> 02:10.830
<i>She's already being controlled!</i>

02:13.520 --> 02:15.040
I'm sorry.

02:17.270 --> 02:18.770
Age manipulation!

02:21.130 --> 02:23.030
Sleep, child.

03:59.440 --> 04:01.870
Everyone misunderstands Jouno.

04:08.710 --> 04:10.520
Jouno is cold.

04:10.520 --> 04:14.770
But in fact, he despises tyranny 
and protects the powerless.

04:15.350 --> 04:19.100
I'll ask again. Tell me where Jouno is.

04:19.110 --> 04:22.110
Episode 58

04:19.110 --> 04:22.110
<b>Land of Inhuman Demons (Part 1)</b>

04:22.570 --> 04:27.460
My correct course of action ought 
to be going after that vampire.

04:28.020 --> 04:32.130
But for just five minutes I turn my 
attention not to justice, but to Jouno.

04:32.780 --> 04:33.840
Answer me!

04:34.190 --> 04:35.590
Where is Jouno?

04:38.690 --> 04:40.530
<i>Message to the Hunting Dogs.</i>

04:40.530 --> 04:42.540
<i>I've captured one of the Detective Agents.</i>

04:43.690 --> 04:46.940
I'll hereby torture him into 
revealing the enemy's plans.

04:46.940 --> 04:50.670
Hold off the other members of the 
Agency so they don't interfere.

04:50.970 --> 04:51.880
Understood.

04:53.100 --> 04:54.650
The radio's working again.

04:55.230 --> 04:58.150
Torture?

04:58.520 --> 04:59.660
Correct.

04:59.660 --> 05:03.120
I sympathize, but your comrade is doomed.

05:07.030 --> 05:09.810
I have to help.

05:11.090 --> 05:12.180
How?

05:25.080 --> 05:26.340
What the...

05:26.830 --> 05:28.260
What just happened to me?

05:31.870 --> 05:33.810
I have to help.

05:34.210 --> 05:36.130
I have to help.

05:36.130 --> 05:38.000
I have to help.

05:38.000 --> 05:39.690
I have to help.

05:46.190 --> 05:47.100
Bastard!

05:48.500 --> 05:50.120
Do not mock me!

05:57.640 --> 06:02.170
Oh, Kunikida-san, when I went 
to work with Kenji-kun today...

06:02.750 --> 06:07.330
There was a tough-looking 
man who was strangely kind.

06:07.740 --> 06:09.000
I'm not surprised.

06:09.710 --> 06:12.630
There's a certain unwritten law in Yokohama.

06:12.970 --> 06:15.850
<b>You must never anger Kenji</b>

06:13.490 --> 06:15.840
You must never anger Kenji.

06:16.160 --> 06:18.470
<i>Our</i> docile Kenji-kun?

06:18.470 --> 06:19.470
That's right.

06:19.940 --> 06:21.260
It's odd, isn't it?

06:21.660 --> 06:24.280
In fact, he's not docile at all.

06:24.280 --> 06:25.600
Just the opposite.

06:26.460 --> 06:29.360
There was a flood in a village 
in the Tohoku region.

06:29.980 --> 06:33.080
The mudslide it caused was 
the worst in fifty years.

06:33.080 --> 06:36.000
It was so severe that maps 
later needed to be rewritten.

06:37.540 --> 06:40.540
But the village was practically untouched.

06:41.340 --> 06:45.110
The president went to investigate 
and found the reason why.

06:45.580 --> 06:47.510
The village was left unharmed

06:47.510 --> 06:51.500
because something had changed the 
direction of the coming mudslide.

06:51.750 --> 06:54.980
It was a boy from the village.

06:54.980 --> 06:57.930
Kenji had redirected the mudslide.

06:58.670 --> 07:01.330
He had gouged out the earth, 
as though he were a giant god

07:01.330 --> 07:02.870
who'd thrown a giant boulder.

07:02.870 --> 07:04.540
A boulder?

07:04.540 --> 07:05.360
With his bare hands?

07:05.800 --> 07:07.130
That's right.

07:07.130 --> 07:09.820
His childhood friend was 
buried alive by the mud.

07:10.100 --> 07:13.380
He says he has no memory of 
what happened after that.

07:15.020 --> 07:18.880
His special ability grants him the 
power of the forces of mother nature.

07:18.880 --> 07:21.870
He merely holds it in with 
his tame personality.

07:22.460 --> 07:27.500
When danger and anger and looming 
nightmares leave him cornered,

07:28.010 --> 07:29.590
<i>it</i> reveals itself.

07:30.440 --> 07:32.770
The fury contained within all creation.

07:33.270 --> 07:35.010
An eruption and a tsunami.

07:36.210 --> 07:38.930
Though it wouldn't do for him 
to be angry all the time,

07:38.930 --> 07:41.390
<b>Gurrrgle</b>

07:39.290 --> 07:41.680
so he gets hungry instead.

07:41.680 --> 07:44.510
Which means, when Kenji-kun 
gets <i>really{i0} angry...</i>

07:45.040 --> 07:46.550
You understand, don't you?

07:46.810 --> 07:51.030
Who could stop an eruption 
with their bare hands?

08:01.370 --> 08:02.630
Kill me.

08:04.020 --> 08:06.300
I ought to have pursued justice.

08:06.750 --> 08:09.040
Thinking it over with a calm mind,

08:09.040 --> 08:13.760
Jouno would have never asked me 
to abandon the mission to save him.

08:15.320 --> 08:20.930
I misjudged my friend, misjudged justice, 
and misjudged the enemy.

08:20.930 --> 08:22.440
And this is the result.

08:23.130 --> 08:25.660
I'm not worthy of being a Hunting Dog.

08:26.610 --> 08:27.580
Kill me.

08:48.420 --> 08:50.970
Let's find that person together.

08:53.290 --> 08:59.010
Thinking it over with a calm mind, 
I have no reason to be angry at you.

08:59.960 --> 09:01.530
Is that so?

09:05.020 --> 09:06.860
What about you?

09:22.360 --> 09:23.980
But first...

09:24.410 --> 09:27.120
I used up too much strength.

09:27.410 --> 09:29.530
Let me rest a bit.

09:29.530 --> 09:30.420
Yeah...

09:30.420 --> 09:31.950
Me, too.

09:34.050 --> 09:35.790
I'm Tetchou.

09:36.710 --> 09:37.780
You?

09:38.220 --> 09:39.750
Kenji.

09:40.140 --> 09:41.200
Kenji.

09:42.510 --> 09:44.330
To have learned that name...

09:45.150 --> 09:47.400
is my greatest 
accomplishment of the day.

09:51.370 --> 09:53.480
Is this really safe?

09:53.920 --> 09:56.610
It's the master of gravity, 
Nakahara Chuuya, that we're up against.

09:56.970 --> 10:00.500
He's way more powerful 
in combat than we are.

10:00.780 --> 10:02.290
It'll be fine!

10:02.290 --> 10:06.750
I've been thinking of ways to kill Chuuya 
every day for the past seven years.

10:07.610 --> 10:09.960
Besides, I have an angel coming with me.

10:09.960 --> 10:11.310
An angel?

10:11.930 --> 10:13.660
You said the same thing earlier, too.

10:15.590 --> 10:17.540
An angel whispered so in my ear.

10:17.860 --> 10:21.180
Is that something you've been told 
by an accomplice on the outside?

10:21.180 --> 10:23.960
You're pretty sharp for a three-year-old.

10:30.430 --> 10:33.730
You're right. I've been 
in contact with Ango.

10:34.510 --> 10:40.610
I quantify the information I want to 
send him and encode it as a heart rate.

10:41.330 --> 10:47.570
A sensor in my body detects it,
 and Ango decodes it.

10:48.010 --> 10:49.240
You're lying.

10:49.470 --> 10:52.110
At least, that's only half of the truth.

10:52.510 --> 10:55.500
There's a flaw to that method.

10:56.040 --> 10:59.700
That method would only allow 
you to send information.

10:59.700 --> 11:01.190
It's a one-way street.

11:01.870 --> 11:03.810
What about information from the surface?

11:03.810 --> 11:05.220
Good observation.

11:05.660 --> 11:07.670
Of course, I have my ways.

11:07.670 --> 11:11.380
I have ways to receive information that 
not even Fyodor would see through.

11:11.380 --> 11:12.710
Wanna take a guess?

11:13.440 --> 11:15.870
If you get it, you're superior to Fyodor!

11:22.810 --> 11:24.140
<i>So easy.</i>

11:24.140 --> 11:25.950
<i>He's the Atsushi-kun type.</i>

11:26.240 --> 11:29.450
<i>How is Dazai getting information 
from the outside?</i>

11:30.210 --> 11:33.130
<i>It couldn't be letters or hidden radio.</i>

11:33.130 --> 11:35.930
<i>The prison is thorough with its checks.</i>

11:36.410 --> 11:38.220
<i>Some kind of special ability, then?</i>

11:38.680 --> 11:40.430
<i>Telepathy, maybe?</i>

11:40.910 --> 11:42.350
<i>No, that wouldn't do it.</i>

11:42.350 --> 11:45.500
<i>Dazai's ability would nullify any telepathy.</i>

11:46.380 --> 11:48.220
<i>What could be the answer?</i>

11:49.320 --> 11:51.510
This isn't the time to for a quiz!

11:51.510 --> 11:52.610
We need to hurry.

11:52.610 --> 11:54.030
Just tell me!

11:54.030 --> 11:56.070
We need to get out before Fyodor does!

11:56.070 --> 11:58.120
I'm not escaping.

11:58.120 --> 11:59.430
Huh?

11:59.430 --> 12:00.540
What are you talking about?

12:00.950 --> 12:03.040
Are you finally unhinged?

12:03.040 --> 12:05.250
How do we win if you aren't going to escape?

12:05.720 --> 12:07.240
It's simple.

12:07.600 --> 12:12.120
We kill Fyodor before the end of the game.

12:13.870 --> 12:16.000
<i>Invalid code.</i>

12:17.450 --> 12:20.210
<i>Critical breach of detention.</i>

12:20.210 --> 12:22.450
<i>Engaging lockdown sequence.</i>

12:23.390 --> 12:24.370
Chuuya-san!

12:29.640 --> 12:32.850
The walls of Mersault are made 
of an anti-Gifted metal.

12:33.330 --> 12:36.810
Not even Chuuya will get through it in time.

12:36.810 --> 12:38.740
Chuuya is strong.

12:38.740 --> 12:40.060
That's why...

12:41.440 --> 12:42.820
We'll defeat him from here.

12:43.220 --> 12:46.410
This is the central surveillance room.

12:46.860 --> 12:48.810
<i>Warning. Warning.</i>

12:48.810 --> 12:51.640
<i>This flooding process cannot be interrupted.</i>

12:56.650 --> 12:58.420
The circuitry's already shot.

12:59.000 --> 13:02.430
Once the door's been closed, 
it never opens again.

13:02.430 --> 13:05.140
And there's no way to stop the flooding.

13:05.140 --> 13:07.020
Wait... What are you doing?

13:07.390 --> 13:11.230
This place isn't called the world's 
most secure prison for nothing.

13:11.230 --> 13:12.910
Don't open that door!

13:12.910 --> 13:14.800
It leads to the surveillance control room!

13:15.250 --> 13:18.150
Do you want us to be killed 
by the armed guards inside?!

13:18.150 --> 13:19.510
I already opened it.

13:30.610 --> 13:31.740
You're kidding...

13:35.300 --> 13:37.460
They're all done.

13:38.770 --> 13:40.270
Did you do this?

13:40.810 --> 13:43.340
But we opened the door just now...

13:44.930 --> 13:46.600
How did you do this?!

13:46.600 --> 13:47.940
I told you...

13:48.430 --> 13:50.340
I stopped time.

13:54.120 --> 13:56.220
This is not good.

13:57.440 --> 13:59.310
You stopped time?

13:59.730 --> 14:01.120
That's impossible.

14:01.120 --> 14:03.810
Yours is a nullifying ability.

14:03.810 --> 14:05.150
Don't mess with me!

14:05.150 --> 14:08.420
Mersault is a trade show 
for dangerous Gifted.

14:08.710 --> 14:11.330
Gifted from all around the world are here.

14:11.760 --> 14:14.050
And <i>she's</i> among them.

14:15.280 --> 14:17.250
A Gifted criminal.

14:17.610 --> 14:19.990
The world's most successful thief.

14:20.380 --> 14:24.350
She was arrested when she stole eight 
military secrets in South America.

14:24.810 --> 14:27.710
Her special ability is fascinating.

14:29.270 --> 14:34.950
For just a few seconds... 
she can stop all time around her.

14:36.340 --> 14:39.890
She can affect a radius several 
kilometers around her.

14:40.160 --> 14:43.350
She and Ango made a plea deal.

14:43.790 --> 14:48.820
In exchange for a shortened sentence, 
she would stop time every morning.

14:49.180 --> 14:52.100
And only the number of times 
Ango instructs her to.

14:53.070 --> 14:55.120
<i>What's the point of that?</i>

14:55.710 --> 14:58.260
<i>She's restrained, isn't she?</i>

14:58.260 --> 15:01.370
<i>So what use would it be 
for her to stop time?</i>

15:02.190 --> 15:04.390
<i>With time being stopped, 
so is consciousness.</i>

15:05.000 --> 15:09.720
<i>Thus, no one even knows 
that time stopped.</i>

15:13.820 --> 15:14.970
Hang on...

15:15.550 --> 15:17.260
You cancel her special ability!

15:17.260 --> 15:18.640
Bingo.

15:18.920 --> 15:22.230
I, alone, can move while time is stopped.

15:22.230 --> 15:26.600
And while time was stopped,
 I took control of the security room.

15:27.170 --> 15:29.780
Knocking out the guards
 while they couldn't move

15:29.780 --> 15:32.580
was easier than beating up 
a sleeping monkey.

15:33.030 --> 15:34.490
<i>This man...</i>

15:34.490 --> 15:35.530
Now, then...

15:36.250 --> 15:39.610
That gives you the answer to that 
homework I gave you, doesn't it?

15:39.610 --> 15:40.510
I see.

15:40.950 --> 15:43.840
That's how you get 
information from the outside.

15:43.840 --> 15:44.830
Yup.

15:44.830 --> 15:49.890
The duration and frequency of 
the pauses is a code in itself.

15:50.250 --> 15:51.660
You get it, don't you?

15:51.990 --> 15:55.310
No one else can receive 
messages with that code.

15:55.850 --> 15:59.630
<i>In other words, Fyodor never stood 
a chance from the beginning.</i>

16:00.080 --> 16:04.330
<i>And Dazai took control of the 
security room and changed the passcodes,</i>

16:04.330 --> 16:06.010
<i>locking Fyodor in.</i>

16:06.620 --> 16:10.370
<i>That's why we were wandering around in the 
opposite direction of the floor exit.</i>

16:10.370 --> 16:11.980
<i>It was to come here!</i>

16:12.340 --> 16:14.940
Everything was as he'd planned.

16:18.620 --> 16:20.490
Can you hear me, Fyodor?

16:20.870 --> 16:23.120
<i>How do you feel about 
your imminent drowning?</i>

16:23.120 --> 16:25.570
<i>You can't kill me.</i>

16:25.570 --> 16:29.260
I like that response,
but how will you escape?

16:29.660 --> 16:33.140
You can't use your special ability. 
The door's indestructible.

16:33.460 --> 16:39.130
<i>And Chuuya's gravity affects what he touches, 
so it's not great for powders or water.</i>

16:39.130 --> 16:41.650
<i>So it must be with your ability, then?</i>

16:41.650 --> 16:43.640
I'd love to see it,
 if that's what you're thinking.

16:44.030 --> 16:48.640
<i>I suspect your ability isn't of the kind 
that'll get you out of this situation, though.</i>

16:48.900 --> 16:50.890
That's why I chose this trap.

16:51.210 --> 16:52.380
<i>He's going to win.</i>

16:52.910 --> 16:57.410
<i>At this rate, Dazai is going to take out 
those two superhumans single-handedly.</i>

16:58.130 --> 17:00.670
Chuuya, it looks like this is goodbye.

17:01.480 --> 17:03.850
<i>It's a shame that it had to happen this way.</i>

17:03.850 --> 17:05.660
<i>It's been seven years since we met.</i>

17:05.660 --> 17:08.310
<i>We never did get along, did we?</i>

17:09.190 --> 17:10.040
But...

17:12.370 --> 17:17.600
Come to think of it now, there were 
times when we understood each other.

17:20.010 --> 17:21.150
For example...

17:39.900 --> 17:42.200
Sorry, I couldn't think of anything.

17:42.200 --> 17:43.410
Anyway...

17:43.830 --> 17:44.780
Goodbye!

18:01.110 --> 18:02.430
There it is!

18:02.890 --> 18:05.230
This carriage has no horse.

18:05.230 --> 18:06.150
Car, you mean.

18:06.580 --> 18:08.000
A cleaning crew's.

18:10.850 --> 18:12.050
Where are we?

18:12.050 --> 18:15.630
It isn't just passengers who 
go through the airport.

18:15.630 --> 18:18.080
There are hundreds of shops in the airport.

18:18.080 --> 18:21.150
There has to be a way to get 
their stuff in and out, right?

18:21.560 --> 18:25.120
The enemy won't have as many eyes there.

18:25.430 --> 18:27.830
And you can escape the 
lockdown through there?

18:27.830 --> 18:30.230
I'm sure they'll check the driver,

18:30.230 --> 18:33.720
but they can't have the time 
to sift through all the cargo.

18:34.130 --> 18:38.260
All we have to do is 
hide in here and wait.

18:38.260 --> 18:41.850
The cleaning crew will take us outside.

18:41.850 --> 18:43.160
I see.

18:43.160 --> 18:45.210
I'm impressed, girl.

18:45.210 --> 18:46.400
Of course.

18:46.400 --> 18:48.560
I'm a hero of justice!

18:50.180 --> 18:51.640
Wake up, Atsushi-kun.

18:52.350 --> 18:53.440
<i>Who is that?</i>

18:53.440 --> 18:54.420
Wake up.

18:54.420 --> 18:55.660
There's no time.

18:55.660 --> 18:56.680
<i>Wake up?</i>

18:57.290 --> 19:00.120
<i>What's happened to me?</i>

19:00.120 --> 19:01.080
Atsushi-kun!

19:07.940 --> 19:09.640
Say, Bra-chan...

19:10.330 --> 19:12.500
That sword hurts, doesn't it?

19:12.500 --> 19:14.330
Want me to help you find 
a way to take it out?

19:15.110 --> 19:16.990
Foolish peasant.

19:16.990 --> 19:18.350
Hold it.

19:18.350 --> 19:20.310
I don't like where this is going.

19:20.630 --> 19:25.590
Break this seal, and I, demon incarnate,

19:25.590 --> 19:29.190
will be free to rule this 
world with darkness!

19:29.940 --> 19:31.820
Yeah, yeah, here we go again.

19:32.290 --> 19:35.200
So what's up with that sword, anyway?

19:35.630 --> 19:37.760
It's all because of that sword, isn't it?

19:38.160 --> 19:41.280
This sword was formerly a human.

19:42.280 --> 19:46.000
Hundreds of years ago, a Gifted died,

19:46.000 --> 19:49.700
and their flesh was turned 
into metal by their ability.

19:49.700 --> 19:52.720
That was reforged into a sword.

19:53.560 --> 19:57.000
Into this Holy Sword Sorslevni.

19:57.310 --> 20:00.030
Their special ability carries 
on even in death.

20:00.030 --> 20:03.220
It is the ability to 
merge flesh with ability.

20:03.790 --> 20:06.060
Flesh and ability?

20:06.060 --> 20:07.350
Indeed.

20:07.350 --> 20:11.150
They exist on two different planes and 
his ability was a means to connect them.

20:11.150 --> 20:15.400
It allows a special ability to be controlled 
as though it's a part of the body.

20:15.400 --> 20:18.600
A super ability transcending 
the laws of this world.

20:18.600 --> 20:21.080
That is what I'm impaled upon.

20:21.560 --> 20:26.370
The tip of the sword 
grows roots in my brain.

20:26.370 --> 20:27.820
And at the same time...

20:28.530 --> 20:33.370
The hand that wields the sword 
is imprinted with a holy seal.

20:33.930 --> 20:38.100
And the seal is now in Fukuchi's palm.

20:38.100 --> 20:42.080
Thus, he alone can use my powers.

20:42.080 --> 20:43.220
Bra-chan...

20:43.220 --> 20:45.310
You know a lot, don't you?

20:45.310 --> 20:46.850
Of course I do.

20:46.850 --> 20:50.850
This is the second time
 I've been impaled by this sword.

20:54.310 --> 20:55.680
Punish him!

20:56.570 --> 20:59.280
Punish the enemy of God!

21:02.680 --> 21:04.030
Please...

21:04.030 --> 21:05.100
Spare the people.

21:05.490 --> 21:06.980
Spare my subjects.

21:07.310 --> 21:09.740
Silence, demon!

21:12.700 --> 21:14.220
Bra-chan...

21:14.220 --> 21:16.620
Why do you look so sad?

21:17.140 --> 21:18.450
It's nothing.

21:18.890 --> 21:22.420
A vassal needs not know the 
turmoil within a lord.

21:23.770 --> 21:24.780
Again...

21:24.780 --> 21:25.750
Vassal?

21:26.190 --> 21:27.890
Do you mean me?

21:27.890 --> 21:28.880
Indeed.

21:28.880 --> 21:33.030
Though, since you carry me, 
perhaps you are not a vassal but a horse.

21:33.470 --> 21:35.590
Want me to drown you in a bathtub?

21:35.590 --> 21:36.750
A bathtub?

21:36.750 --> 21:40.390
Is that how the people of this time 
pay their respects to a king?

21:40.390 --> 21:42.100
Valuable knowledge.

21:42.100 --> 21:44.040
Sure must be empowering to be so oblivious.

22:02.960 --> 22:04.660
Run, child.

22:06.370 --> 22:07.470
Run, now!

23:36.020 --> 23:40.010
Next Episode
Episode 59

23:36.020 --> 23:40.010
<i>Land of Inhuman Demons (Part 2)</i>
